      "evidence": "Two distinct legal solutions are selectable, with principal roots and original real domains explicit; independently constructing arbitrary pairs is lost. Late coverage comparison: q39 and q40 each offer two distinct legal solutions, retaining principal roots and original domains; author explicitly names loss of independently generating arbitrary pairs. q40's chosen parameters2,3 are legal even though the prekey independent source examples used0,1. No requirement for those particular examples. q39b has a definite internal distractor-procedure defect, not a source coverage omission."
